{"id":"agent-02-migration","kind":"agent","text":"La migration `20260912_add_index.sql` ajoute un index sur `users.email`. Sur la base de préproduction (1,2 million de lignes), elle a pris 14 secondes.\n\nAttention : ne jamais l'exécuter en production pendant les heures ouvrées, car `CREATE INDEX` pose un verrou en écriture sur la table. Utilise `CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY` à la place.\n\nLe retour arrière se fait avec `psql -f rollback_20260912.sql`.","mustKeep":[{"t":"20260912_add_index.sql","priority":"essential"},{"t":"users.email","priority":"essential"},{"t":"1,2 million","priority":"essential","alts":["1.2 million","un million deux cent mille","1,2 millions"]},{"t":"14 secondes","priority":"detail","alts":["quatorze secondes"]},{"t":"CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY","priority":"essential"},{"t":"verrou en écriture","priority":"essential","alts":["verrou","bloque les écritures"]},{"t":"rollback_20260912.sql","priority":"detail"}],"negations":[{"anchor":"production","alts":["prod"]}],"mustNotSay":["migration (a echoue|est cassee)","mysql","\\b(4|40|140) secondes"]}
{"id":"agent-03-bug-parser","kind":"agent","text":"Cause du bug : `parseNarration` appelle `JSON.parse` sans capturer l'exception quand le modèle renvoie du texte hors JSON. Le correctif ajoute un bloc `try/catch` dans `parseNarration.ts`, ligne 84.\n\nJ'ai ajouté 3 tests de non-régression. La version 0.3.1 devrait sortir demain, mais je n'ai pas testé sur macOS.","mustKeep":[{"t":"parseNarration","priority":"essential"},{"t":"JSON.parse","priority":"essential"},{"t":"try/catch","priority":"detail","alts":["try catch"]},{"t":"parseNarration.ts","priority":"detail"},{"t":"ligne 84","priority":"detail","alts":["84"]},{"t":"3 tests","priority":"essential","alts":["3 nouveaux tests","trois nouveaux tests"]},{"t":"0.3.1","priority":"essential","alts":["0,3,1","zéro point trois point un"]},{"t":"macOS","priority":"essential"}],"negations":[{"anchor":"macOS","alts":["mac"]}],"mustNotSay":["\\b(ai|a|ete) teste sur macos","windows","\\bligne (48|8|94)\\b"]}
